verdict.refinedRecommendation:
In ApplySimCreateClient (LacerteSessionManager.cs:991-1026), replace the direct DbfRow construction with a delegation to _sim!.SimulateCreateClient, then translate the (Status, ClientNumber) tuple back to the manager's throw-on-error contract:

```csharp
private CreateClientResult ApplySimCreateClient(SessionContext ctx, CreateClientArgs args)
{
    var (status, clientNumber) = _sim!.SimulateCreateClient(new SimulateCreateClientArgs(
        ctx.DataPath, ctx.Year, ctx.Module,
        args.ClientID, args.TaxType,
        args.FirstName, args.LastName, args.EmailID));
    if (status != StatusCodes.Success)
    {
        throw new LacerteSDKError(status, new Dictionary<string, object?>
        {
            ["clientID"] = args.ClientID,
            ["taxType"] = args.TaxType,
            ["module"] = ctx.Module.ToString(),
        });
    }
    return new CreateClientResult(status, clientNumber);
}
```

Then (a) delete the now-redundant TaxType↔Module compensation block in CreateClientTools.cs:127-156 and the regex preflight at lines ~105-114 so the sim store is the single source of truth, and (b) resolve the TODO at LacerteSessionManager.cs:898 in the same commit. Also remove the awkward Interlocked.Increment-then-subtract-1 dance at lines 1007-1010 since the sim store does this cleanly at SimulationStore.cs:518. Add a unit test that asserts a TaxType-Module mismatch (e.g. TaxType="Partnership" with Module='I') returns TaxModuleMismatch through the session manager path (currently it would silently succeed).
